WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.067 --> 00:00:02.902
So in this box is
milestone piece of tech.

00:00:05.104 --> 00:00:07.006
I've never actually seen
one of these.

00:00:07.006 --> 00:00:08.241
Oh my god.

00:00:08.808 --> 00:00:10.243
[awe noise]

00:00:10.243 --> 00:00:11.611
This is definitely
older than me.

00:00:11.611 --> 00:00:12.812
This is functioning?

00:00:12.812 --> 00:00:14.514
[laughing]
What is this?

00:00:16.148 --> 00:00:18.184
[music]

00:00:18.184 --> 00:00:20.086
Let's see what people
think about you.

00:00:20.153 --> 00:00:22.021
I'm Marques Brownlee
and I review

00:00:22.021 --> 00:00:24.357
dope new tech but on this
show

00:00:24.357 --> 00:00:27.026
I'm rewinding the clock to
discover the tech of the

00:00:27.026 --> 00:00:29.362
past that changed
our lives forever.

00:00:29.929 --> 00:00:32.932
Sega Genesis in the
original box.

00:00:32.932 --> 00:00:34.634
The first ever cell phone.

00:00:34.634 --> 00:00:36.870
The revolutionary 
JVC camcorder

00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:38.537
Polaroid sx-70

00:00:38.638 --> 00:00:39.605
Sony Walkman

00:00:39.605 --> 00:00:42.941
And the original,
the 1984 Mac.

00:00:42.941 --> 00:00:43.443
[music]

00:00:43.443 --> 00:00:45.444
The DynaTAC 8000x

00:00:45.444 --> 00:00:48.481
was ten of today's
smartphones thick.

00:00:48.481 --> 00:00:50.449
Tactile buttons.

00:00:50.449 --> 00:00:51.217
[buttons clicking]

00:00:51.217 --> 00:00:53.152
Immensely satisfying.

00:00:53.552 --> 00:00:55.221
Today
we test a Walkmans

00:00:55.221 --> 00:00:57.557
wearability playability
durability

00:00:58.224 --> 00:00:59.125
[boom]

00:00:59.125 --> 00:00:59.659
It did pretty well.

00:00:59.659 --> 00:01:00.660
[static noise]

00:01:00.693 --> 00:01:01.627
Is it rolling?

00:01:01.627 --> 00:01:02.628
I'm kinda wondering if this

00:01:02.628 --> 00:01:03.696
brings back any
memories?

00:01:03.730 --> 00:01:05.831
Am I here because
of my advanced age?

00:01:05.831 --> 00:01:06.966
In the 90s I would have

00:01:06.966 --> 00:01:08.567
been a Genesis gamer.

00:01:08.567 --> 00:01:11.571
I remember wait till
I get this on these

00:01:11.571 --> 00:01:12.572
mother ---

00:01:12.572 --> 00:01:15.141
[laughing]

00:01:15.141 --> 00:01:17.577
128k people.

00:01:17.577 --> 00:01:20.046
And k stands for kilobyte?

00:01:20.046 --> 00:01:20.847
Yes!

00:01:20.913 --> 00:01:23.416
[laughter]
Okay. Got it.

00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:25.484
Kids today.

00:01:26.018 --> 00:01:27.687
They don't make em like
they used to.

00:01:27.687 --> 00:01:29.355
And I gotta say,
I have a lot more respect now 

00:01:29.388 --> 00:01:30.523
for just how much
this tech

00:01:30.523 --> 00:01:32.592
was at the very
bleeding edge

00:01:32.592 --> 00:01:33.759
at that time.

00:01:33.759 --> 00:01:34.761
Catch you guys at
the next one.

00:01:34.761 --> 00:01:35.994
Thanks for watching.

00:01:35.994 --> 00:01:39.165
[music]

00:01:40.432 --> 00:01:50.276
[music]

